---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";
import CTA from "../../components/CTA.astro";
import AuditClose from "../../components/AuditClose.astro";
import FAQ from "../../components/FAQ.astro";
---

<Site
  page="local"
  title="Local Growth | The Anchorline AI Growth Engine"
  description="Connect your website, local visibility, SEO/AEO/GEO, reputation, paid demand, lead capture, and follow-up with Anchorline's Local Growth configuration."
>
  <section class="container page-hero market-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE GROWTH ENGINE / LOCAL CONFIGURATION</p><h1>
        Be found.<br />Be chosen.<br /><span class="accent-word"
          >Follow through.</span>
      </h1><p class="hero-lede">
        A growth system built around how local customers find, evaluate, and
        choose a business. Connect the moments between their first search and
        their next step.
      </p><CTA
        href="/growth-audit/?pathway=local"
        pathway="local"
        location="local-hero"
      />
    </div><div
      class="local-visual"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Illustrative local customer path connecting search visibility, reputation, website, inquiry, and follow-up. Not a real map or ranking report."
    >
      <span class="mono visual-index">LOCAL / VISIBILITY TO OPPORTUNITY</span
      ><div class="map-grid">
        <i class="map-street street-one"></i><i class="map-street street-two"
        ></i><i class="map-street street-three"></i><div
          class="map-node node-search"
        >
          Search
        </div><div class="map-node node-trust">Reputation</div><div
          class="map-business"
        >
          YOUR<br />BUSINESS
        </div><div class="map-node node-web">Website</div><div
          class="map-node node-follow"
        >
          Follow-up
        </div><span class="map-radius"></span>
      </div><small class="artifact-note"
        >Illustrative customer journey, not geographic or ranking data.</small>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container editorial-split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">FOR LOCAL & SERVICE BUSINESSES</p><h2>
        Visibility opens<br />the door.<br /><span class="muted-heading"
          >The experience matters next.</span>
      </h2>
    </div><div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="large-copy">Being found is only part of being chosen.</p><p>
        Customers compare your website, reputation, clarity, and responsiveness.
        A strong acquisition system connects those moments instead of optimizing
        each in isolation.
      </p><p>
        Local Growth brings website improvement, Google and local presence,
        search readability, reputation, appropriate paid demand, capture, and
        follow-up into one configured engagement.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section engine-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE LOCAL GROWTH PATH</p><h2>
        A connected journey<br />from discovery to inquiry.
      </h2><div class="local-journey">
        <article>
          <span class="mono">01 / DISCOVER</span><h3>Show up clearly.</h3><p>
            Website foundations, local search visibility, and useful content for
            search and answer engines.
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span class="mono">02 / EVALUATE</span><h3>Earn the next click.</h3><p
          >
            Clear services, credible reputation, helpful answers, and a mobile
            experience that makes sense.
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span class="mono">03 / CONTACT</span><h3>Make action easy.</h3><p>
            Focused landing pages, calls to action, and lead capture connected
            to the right destination.
          </p>
        </article><article>
          <span class="mono">04 / FOLLOW THROUGH</span><h3>
            Keep the opportunity moving.
          </h3><p>
            Defined follow-up responsibilities, appropriate automation, and
            meaningful conversion measurement.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container evidence-composition">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">EXAMPLE / NOT A CLIENT CASE STUDY</p><h2>
        Look beyond<br />a better-looking website.
      </h2><p class="section-intro">
        A local growth review examines the path a potential customer actually
        takes. Visual improvement matters when it supports understanding,
        confidence, and action.
      </p>
    </div><article class="example-board local-example">
      <div class="mono example-label">ILLUSTRATIVE LOCAL REVIEW</div><div
        class="example-row"
      >
        <span>Findability</span><p>
          Can a relevant customer discover and understand the business?
        </p>
      </div><div class="example-row">
        <span>Confidence</span><p>
          Does the experience provide clear, truthful reasons to choose it?
        </p>
      </div><div class="example-row">
        <span>Conversion</span><p>
          Is the next step obvious and practical on a phone?
        </p>
      </div><div class="example-row">
        <span>Response</span><p>
          Is there an accountable path from inquiry to follow-up?
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="section container faq-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">SEARCH, DEMAND & CONVERSION</p><h2>
        Useful capabilities.<br />No magic promises.
      </h2>
    </div><FAQ
      items={[
        [
          "What do SEO, AEO, and GEO mean here?",
          "SEO supports discovery in search engines. AEO makes useful answers easier to understand and retrieve. GEO considers how generative search systems can understand and reference a business. Clear content, technical foundations, and credible evidence matter across them; placement is not guaranteed.",
        ],
        [
          "Does every local business need paid ads?",
          "No. Paid demand should support a clear offer and a working conversion path. The audit may identify website, visibility, reputation, or follow-up improvements as higher priorities.",
        ],
        [
          "Is Local Growth a separate company or product?",
          "No. It is a primary configuration of the Anchorline AI Growth Engine, built around local customer acquisition rather than a B2B account-led sales motion.",
        ],
      ]}
    />
  </section>
  <AuditClose pathway="local" title="Where are local customers dropping off?" />
</Site>
